/**
 * stop_on_pr_close.ts — closing a pull request an agent is working on asks that run to
 * stop, the same way closing its issue does.
 *
 * ## Why a pull request's close has to mean something
 *
 * A run was reviewing a pull request (run 42232540109) when the pull request merged. The
 * merge reached nothing: the run kept going for another nine minutes and stopped only
 * when an unrelated parent issue was closed, which propagated a stop through the issue
 * path below. The structure was right and the coverage was not — `issues: closed` stops
 * a run, and `pull_request_target: closed` did not, for either outcome (#455).
 *
 * ## The mechanism is the existing one
 *
 * No second stop path. `STOP_TAG` in a comment, polled for by the running job, is the
 * only way anything reaches a job's filesystem from outside it — `/stop` and the issue
 * close both work that way. This is one more writer of the same tag.
 *
